# Copied once to ~/.zshrc.local (mode 600), never linked or overwritten by setup.
# Portable non-secret settings belong in the tracked Zsh files.
# For a credential: run `keyset SERVICE_NAME`, then paste into its hidden prompt.
# Load it only where needed with `keyenv VARIABLE_NAME SERVICE_NAME`.
# Examples (enable only after adding the corresponding Keychain item):
# keyenv HF_TOKEN
# keyenv NPM_TOKEN
# keyenv DOCKER_TOKEN
# keyenv DOCKER_HUB_PASSWORD
#
# Prefer `gh auth login` over exporting GH_TOKEN globally; old tokens override
# GitHub CLI's saved login. Prefer AWS profiles/SSO over copied session tokens.
# Keep a password-manager copy of credentials you intend to use on other Macs.
